        "zh-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7938e134-2631-38f7-8ef9-b6fde46ed7be",
                "word": "shenanigan",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c5d973c9-6143-4c9f-95a7-441fdab9b1d3",
                        "entry_id": "7938e134-2631-38f7-8ef9-b6fde46ed7be",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "shenanigans"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78cbfba4-79c7-357e-88b1-3e7354a17bd9",
                        "entry_id": "7938e134-2631-38f7-8ef9-b6fde46ed7be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "欺騙性的詭計或惡作劇；造成不適或煩惱。"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d666c6f-4d52-4161-9cf6-722f1c4066b1",
                                "sense_id": "78cbfba4-79c7-357e-88b1-3e7354a17bd9",
                                "text": "I spotted his next shenanigan – saw it coming – and so avoided being fooled.",
                                "translation": "我發現了他的下一個惡作劇——預見了——因此避免了被愚弄。"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8f38c776-7441-3dc6-a48b-d4249a7c4f59",
                        "entry_id": "7938e134-2631-38f7-8ef9-b6fde46ed7be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "shenanigans 的單數"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "form-of",
                            "rare",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "813d1f6b-91ae-4845-be8b-925ed6125b53",
                                "sense_id": "8f38c776-7441-3dc6-a48b-d4249a7c4f59",
                                "text": "One of Professor [John] Moon's most astonishing \"experiments,\" consisted of holding a watch suspended from a short chain at arm's length, and allowing anyone in the pit to pull pistol and \"blaze away\" at the word \"fire,\" whereupon the watch would most unconscionably disappear. An individual who had attended several evenings and witnessed the \"experiment,\" suspected, in the classic language of the times, that there was something of \"shenanigan\" in it.",
                                "translation": "約翰·穆恩教授最令人震驚的“實驗”之一是，將一塊手錶懸掛在一條短鏈上，距離手臂很遠，然後讓坑里的任何人在聽到“火”這個詞時拔出手槍並“射擊”，然後手錶就會毫無意義地消失。一位參加了數晚的“實驗”並目睹了這一“實驗”的人，用當時的經典語言來說，懷疑其中存在某種“惡作劇”的成分。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5de4a5a-3a85-4860-b5fd-f26b00f35dd2",
                                "sense_id": "8f38c776-7441-3dc6-a48b-d4249a7c4f59",
                                "text": "There are stories still told how money was used and promised, but from the best knowledge I can acquire, I think this is not true. If sharp practice was played, and \"shenanigan\" was used, we, to-day, looking back upon those times, cannot say that evil has come of it.",
                                "translation": "仍然有一些故事講述如何使用和承諾資金，但從我所能獲得的最佳知識來看，我認為這不是真的。如果當時確實存在不正當手段，使用“詭計”，那麼今天我們回顧當時的情況，不能說當時造成了邪惡。"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ]
    }
